        "description": "On the evening of 12 August, the whole of the UK will see its most dramatic partial solar eclipse in nearly three decades.\n\nFrom the UK, the Moon will block out up to 96% of the Sun.\n\nThe same eclipse will be visible across Europe and some will enjoy the ultimate solar spectacle: a total solar eclipse.\n\nIn this video we have everything you need to know about the eclipse and how to watch it safely. \n\nCHAPTERHEADS: \n0:00 - 1:55 - INTRO\n1:56 - 3:45 - Where will the eclipse be visible?\n3:46 - 5:29 - Will the skies be clear?\n5:30 - 8:52 What is it like?\n8:53 - 11:17 - How do I watch safely?\n11:17 - 12:46 - When is the next one?\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#BBCNews",
